    {
      "ply": 37,
      "san": "Nh6+",
      "human_san": "Nh6+",
      "san_match": true,
      "human_comment": "A mistake would be 19. Bxd4 for 19... Bxf5. 19. Nxd4 was also wrong\nbecause of the continuation 19... bxc6 20. Nxc6 Rxe2+ 21. Kxe2 Qe8+ and Black\nis better.",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "Nh6+ is the most accurate move, holding the balance (+0.20, Stockfish:16) in [pv:Nh6+], as Black immediately leaves a piece hanging\u2014always awkward to resolve while the king is in check. Bxd4 was a comparable alternative that leads to equality along [pv:Bxd4 Bxf5 Qxf5 Qxd4 Qd5+], with White's king safe and Black's pieces passive, but the check keeps slightly better practical chances; after 20.Kg8, White's edge can grow.",
      "system_symbol": "!",
      "is_key_moment": true,
      "final_comment": true,
      "both_present": true,
      "human_only": false,
      "system_only": false,
