      "human_comment": "Black resign\ns. Flohr does not tell us how many seconds are left, but probably, at this\npoint he did not need so many of them.",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "Bxf6 is the most accurate move, winning a knight\u2014a lasting material edge\u2014right away, though White's advantage shrinks because a piece is left hanging in return; the line may weaken Black's pawn structure further, while Black could pin a White piece. (+4.31 \u2192 +3.68, Stockfish:16) [pv:Bxf6 Ra8 Bc3 Ra4 d3] Bd3+ was a comparable option that leaves White with a decisive advantage, winning a knight for a pawn and exposing Black's back rank: [pv:Bd3+ Kg8 Nh6+ Kh8 Bxf6]",
